Sval: a host's fingerprinting overrides beat its site's

nsRFPService keys first-party overrides by the base domain alone, so a
choice made for one host could not be told from its site's. A first-party
lookup takes the key of the page's host, or the nearest name above it, that
has an entry, before the base domain's (SvalRFPService.cpp).

diff --git a/toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/nsRFPService.cpp b/toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/nsRFPService.cpp
index 994e1cb4c6..fa6686da50 100644
--- a/toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/nsRFPService.cpp
+++ b/toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/nsRFPService.cpp
@@ -3024,6 +3024,10 @@ Maybe<RFPTargetSet> nsRFPService::GetOverriddenFingerprintingSettingsForURI(
   //   2. {first-party domain}: First-party contexts that load the given
   //   first-party domain.
   if (!aThirdPartyURI) {
+    // Sval: a host's own entry, a choice made for that host, beats its site's.
+    SvalRFPService::NarrowFirstPartyDomain(overrides, aFirstPartyURI,
+                                           isBaseline, firstPartyDomain);
+
     // Test the {first-party domain, *} scope.
     key.Assign(firstPartyDomain);
     key.Append(FP_OVERRIDES_DOMAIN_KEY_DELIMITER);
